# CODEOWNERS — undercurrentai/aegis-policy
#
# Default + path-specific ownership for the verifier policy + trust roots.
# Per cosmic-flute §17 Critical 3: this repo has a stricter trust model than
# the implementing repos. Every change requires explicit owner approval.
#
# Trust-spine owner is the TEAM @undercurrentai/security-reviewers (created
# 2026-07-29, the growth path this header always documented). The point of the
# team indirection: adding a reviewer is now a team-membership change — an
# org-settings operation touching no tracked file — instead of a CODEOWNERS
# edit that itself costs a §34.17.2 break-glass cycle. Sole member today is
# @ThermoclineLeviathan, so behavior is UNCHANGED until a second human joins;
# GitHub still forbids self-approval, so the bypass cycle remains the merge
# path for trust-spine PRs exactly until that day. (A second account owned by
# the same person was considered and REFUSED — see docs/roadmap.md.)
# Future hardening once 2-of-N is real: required_approving_review_count: 2 on
# `keys/`, `schema/`, `policy/` paths.

# Default — routine (non-trust-spine, non-dep-file) changes may be code-owner-
# approved by the §44 Phase 2 machine-user @aegis-auto-reviewer (3-AI consensus
# auto-approve via .github/workflows/ai-second-review.yml aggregator-approve job;
# cosmic-flute §54). Last-match-wins: @aegis-auto-reviewer is on the `*` line ONLY
# and is EXCLUDED from every trust-spine + carve-out + dep-file entry below, so
# those PRs still require a @undercurrentai/security-reviewers member (today:
# only @ThermoclineLeviathan) + the manual §34.17.2 bypass cycle.
*                                  @ThermoclineLeviathan @aegis-auto-reviewer

# Trust-material paths — explicit + verbose to make scope obvious
keys/                              @undercurrentai/security-reviewers
schema/                            @undercurrentai/security-reviewers
policy/                            @undercurrentai/security-reviewers
.github/                           @undercurrentai/security-reviewers
.github/workflows/                 @undercurrentai/security-reviewers

# ADRs — architectural changes need owner sign-off
docs/architecture/                 @undercurrentai/security-reviewers

# Maintenance scripts (parity gate is load-bearing)
scripts/                           @undercurrentai/security-reviewers

# Verifier-kit composite Action — externally consumed (uses: undercurrentai/
# aegis-policy/actions/verify-aegis-attestation@<sha>); pins the canonical signing
# keys + policy/verifier-policy-v1.yaml + runs the offline attestation verification.
# Trust-spine material — human-only (closes the actions/ fall-through per QG-§54 audit).
actions/                           @undercurrentai/security-reviewers

# §44 Phase 2 carve-out source-of-truth — human-only (mirrors its self-protection
# glob in .aegis-trust-spine-paths.yaml; the two defense layers stay in lockstep)
/.aegis-trust-spine-paths.yaml     @undercurrentai/security-reviewers

# Supply-chain dep files — human-only (cosmic-flute §54 Q2: close the residual
# auto-approve gap; mirrored in .aegis-trust-spine-paths.yaml trust_spine_globs).
# requirements-dev.txt and requirements-ci.txt (its hash-pinned lockfile — the
# file CI actually installs) exist today; the rest are a forward-proof superset —
# a CODEOWNERS line for an absent path is harmless (matches nothing until created).
/requirements-dev.txt              @undercurrentai/security-reviewers
/requirements-ci.txt               @undercurrentai/security-reviewers
/requirements-aux.txt              @undercurrentai/security-reviewers
/requirements-aux-ci.txt           @undercurrentai/security-reviewers
/requirements-verify.txt           @undercurrentai/security-reviewers
/requirements-verify-ci.txt        @undercurrentai/security-reviewers
/requirements.txt                  @undercurrentai/security-reviewers
/pyproject.toml                    @undercurrentai/security-reviewers
/Makefile                          @undercurrentai/security-reviewers
/package.json                      @undercurrentai/security-reviewers
/package-lock.json                 @undercurrentai/security-reviewers
/setup.py                          @undercurrentai/security-reviewers
/setup.cfg                         @undercurrentai/security-reviewers
/Pipfile                           @undercurrentai/security-reviewers
/poetry.lock                       @undercurrentai/security-reviewers
/tox.ini                           @undercurrentai/security-reviewers

# Root CI / governance config — human-only (closes the root-config fall-through per
# QG-§54 audit: a .gitignore secret-un-ignore + .afa.yaml gate-config edit must be
# human-reviewed, not machine-auto-approved). Mirrored in trust_spine_globs.
/.gitignore                        @undercurrentai/security-reviewers
/.afa.yaml                         @undercurrentai/security-reviewers
/.markdownlint.json                @undercurrentai/security-reviewers

# Test-suite config — controls test SELECTION (markers + addopts). A one-line
# `addopts = -m "not <marker>"` edit can deselect the entire suite while every
# check stays green, so it gets the same human-only treatment as the dep
# manifests. Mirrored in .aegis-trust-spine-paths.yaml. (Introduced in #36
# WITHOUT this protection: a PR touching only pytest.ini fell under `*`, where
# the machine-user IS a code owner, and was auto-approvable — closed here.)
/pytest.ini                        @undercurrentai/security-reviewers
# Root conftest.py: pytest auto-executes it at collection in every CI venv —
# arbitrary code in the required test jobs. Absent today; pre-armed so its
# creation is human-only (matches the trust-spine glob added with it).
/conftest.py                       @undercurrentai/security-reviewers
